cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use HelioFITS Studio in your research, please cite the version you
  used (each release has its own Zenodo DOI) and the JHelioviewer paper it is
  built on. If you use the RHEF filter, please also cite Gilly and Cranmer
  (2025).
type: software
title: HelioFITS Studio
abstract: >-
  HelioFITS Studio is a desktop viewer for solar and heliospheric imagery,
  built around coronagraph and wide-field data. It is an unofficial fork of
  JHelioviewer, the open-source solar image browser of the ESA/NASA
  Helioviewer Project, that adds tools for the outer corona: PUNCH and native
  LASCO data loading, the Helioradial projections, the RHEF radial histogram
  equalizing filter, CME tracking against the CACTus catalog, point cloud
  layers and deep-colour movie export.
authors:
  - given-names: Chris R.
    family-names: Gilly
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0021-9056"
    affiliation: NorthWest Research Associates
repository-code: "https://github.com/GillySpace27/HelioFITS-Studio"
url: "https://gilly.space/heliofits-studio"
license: MPL-2.0
# Concept DOI: always resolves to the newest release; each release also has its own version DOI.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23541893
